{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/386889-when-a-game-hits-home-crying-for-a-character","id":386889,"title":"When a Game hits home. Crying for a character","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-01-30T18:23:58-08:00","id":386889,"title":"When a Game hits home. Crying for a character","content":"I been running a campaing for a year. i did a lot of homebrewing but the game started with a hunter and a nuwisha setting down and ending up as a family (fuck the rules).<br /> they fought in apocalypse and the coyote died with his daughter and son, she was the sole survivor... this game made one player cry, after this we got very close and had something going.<br /> i made both characters appear in my mage game, the nuwisha on a quest to try to save her soul (after she died and ended up in bedlam), with out her he lost his sense of being and didnt laugh anymore, with out him she was driven insane.<br /> during this time , me and her split up, she even stop going to the games for a while. i tried to go back with her but she had someone else already.<br /> <br /> today she went to the game with her boyfriend, she took her character ( as a wraith ) and the coyote ended up dying for her, she had her revenge against the creature that killed her. after that, i described a scene in which she closed her eyes feeling relief (the player started to cry), and i described how somewhere else. in another place, a 5 year old was being bulled by a bunch of kids and was left alone crying, suddenly another kid wearing the coyote's clothes, came by and put a bandage over her knee, saying that he moved in nearby and saw her crying. they introduced each other and he took her back to her house.<br /> my player just started to weep.<br /> <br /> as a storyteller, i felt i did the right thing for finishing that story, afterwards i gave her a letter saying &quot;i dont know if those chars are still togeather or not, if they moved on with their lifes and meet other people, or if they hate each other, or if they are indifferent or they are friends. all i know is that they are in a better place&quot; basically.<br /> <br /> i feel like i closed a chapter in my life, and i still feel bitter and yet longing with some sorrow...but, i feel like i closed an entire chapter of my life now.<br /> <br /> <br /> Have you ever gone through a chars death or some event that defined a moment in your life? something that made you cry or feel utter joy?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-31T11:16:31-08:00","id":387495,"title":"","content":"How about white hot incandescent rage?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-31T18:04:54-08:00","id":387891,"title":"","content":"do elaborate","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-01T09:12:12-08:00","id":388485,"title":"","content":"I wrote a big long post about it and answering your actual question in detail as well (with examples). Hit the wrong button and it's gone.<br /> <br /> So, back to white hot incandescent rage.....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-01T11:15:29-08:00","id":388647,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/386889-when-a-game-hits-home-crying-for-a-character#post386889\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I been running a campaing for a year. i did a lot of homebrewing but the game started with a hunter and a nuwisha setting down and ending up as a family (fuck the rules).<br /> they fought in apocalypse and the coyote died with his daughter and son, she was the sole survivor... this game made one player cry, after this we got very close and had something going.<br /> i made both characters appear in my mage game, the nuwisha on a quest to try to save her soul (after she died and ended up in bedlam), with out her he lost his sense of being and didnt laugh anymore, with out him she was driven insane.<br /> during this time , me and her split up, she even stop going to the games for a while. i tried to go back with her but she had someone else already.<br /> <br /> today she went to the game with her boyfriend, she took her character ( as a wraith ) and the coyote ended up dying for her, she had her revenge against the creature that killed her. after that, i described a scene in which she closed her eyes feeling relief (the player started to cry), and i described how somewhere else. in another place, a 5 year old was being bulled by a bunch of kids and was left alone crying, suddenly another kid wearing the coyote's clothes, came by and put a bandage over her knee, saying that he moved in nearby and saw her crying. they introduced each other and he took her back to her house.<br /> my player just started to weep.<br /> <br /> as a storyteller, i felt i did the right thing for finishing that story, afterwards i gave her a letter saying &quot;i dont know if those chars are still togeather or not, if they moved on with their lifes and meet other people, or if they hate each other, or if they are indifferent or they are friends. all i know is that they are in a better place&quot; basically.<br /> <br /> i feel like i closed a chapter in my life, and i still feel bitter and yet longing with some sorrow...but, i feel like i closed an entire chapter of my life now.<br /> <br /> <br /> Have you ever gone through a chars death or some event that defined a moment in your life? something that made you cry or feel utter joy?</div> </div> </div> </div>What a lovely and touching story.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my DriveThruRPG books at: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?author=Carrie%20Kube\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse....=Carrie%20Kube</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1834-yaoi-huntress-earth","name":"Yaoi Huntress Earth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1834_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"535"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-02T17:47:17-08:00","id":390712,"title":"","content":"Oh yes <i>The Grand Adventures of Stinky Stan</i>. These tales were made by some of the most retarded and brilliant players to grace my tables. Many tears graced the keyboards as were many &quot;Dude. What the fuck?&quot;. Such tales should not be spoken of in the halls of mortal men but let me just say one thing. <b>No campaign will ever be as amazing as that campaign for me.</b> I've done many crazy things from a Hunter who was on the search for vengeance after his wife and daughter were lost to an inhuman vampire who is trying to destroy the Sabbat and fix the world and instead finding the love of his life and going through the trials of having a family. But all of these still fail in comparsion to chronicle that was <i>The Grand Adventures of Stinky Stan</i>.<br /> <br /> For those that die in glory are the truly blessed. You were the hero the city deserved Stan, but not the one it needed right now.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1VN49Y7tH2ZV0l7Hx65RWX1ez-Q9Lst-8ZTyTJeCTpxM/\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerer 20th</a> homebrew and my update to <a href=\"http://immortalthegathering.blogspot.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Highlander: the Gathering</a> for 20th Anniversary edition.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2414-theoutlander523","name":"theoutlander523","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-02T21:09:17-08:00","id":390977,"title":"","content":"Once, during a convention Changeling: the Lost game. On our final ride to battle, the prodigal Queen of Spring was giving our motley safe passage to the apocalyptic battle. The Storyteller just using tone of voice and words made it perfectly clear that this woman was going to die, that she was terrified out of her mind at the thought, and she was going to the front lines anyway. Got misty-eye. After she fell, we swore a Pledge to avenger her, or die trying.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2233-agentwestmer","name":"Agentwestmer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2233_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}